===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰew-|*speh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|god spede}}, {{m|enm|god speid|t=(''adverb'') quickly, speedily; (''interjection'') may God cause (someone) to succeed}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=gọ̄d spẹ̄de, gọ̄̆d-spẹ̄de|pos=phr.'' & ''n|id=MED19001}}</ref><ref name="MED God">{{R:MED Online|subentry=[god] spede|entry=God, god|pos=''n.''(1)|noformat=1|id=MED18945}}</ref> from {{m|enm|god}}, {{m|enm|God|t=(''Christianity'') God; the Eucharist; non-Christian god or goddess; idol; deity, divine being; person or thing honoured as a god}}<ref name="MED God"/> (from {{inh|en|ang|god|t=god}}, ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰew-|t=to pour}}, in the sense of a libation made to a god) + {{m|enm|sped}}, {{m|enm|spede}}, the {{glossary|singular}} {{glossary|subjunctive}} of {{m|enm|speden|t=to achieve one’s goal; to succeed (in something); to fare, get along; to conduct oneself well; to do well, prosper, thrive; to turn out well; to be advantageous, avail; to be of benefit or useful; to assist, help; to help (someone) be successful; to do or complete (something); to travel rapidly; to progress}}<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=spẹ̄den|pos=v|id=MED42062}}</ref> (from {{inh|en|ang|spēdan|t=to succeed}}, ultimately from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*speh₁-|t=to prosper, succeed}}).<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=79693|date=December 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=excl}}</ref>

